        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "Determine the set of real values of \\(a\\) for which both roots of \\(x^2-2(a+1)x+a^2-3a+2=0\\) are positive.",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "For real roots, \\(D=4(5a-1)\\ge0\\), so \\(a\\ge\\frac{1}{5}\\). Also, the sum of roots is \\(2(a+1)>0\\), and the product is \\((a-1)(a-2)>0\\). Combining these gives \\(\\left[\\frac{1}{5},1\\right)\\cup\\left(2,\\infty\\right)\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
        "sort_order": 7,
        "question_data": {
